  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I would like VRChat to support multi-device audio output, so each audio bus can be sent to a different playback device (including virtual audio cables).\n\nThis is mainly useful for videographers, and I understand it may be costly to implement. Please only consider it when you have spare bandwidth.\n\nIt is not a high-priority request for everyday play.\n\nThe idea is to keep the existing volume buses and add an optional output-device assignment for each one: Master/UIMenu/World/Voices/Avatars/ItemsEffects\n\nIf each bus can be routed to its own virtual audio device, creators can capture them as separate tracks in OBS.\n\nOBS recording supports up to 6 audio tracks.\n\nThis would help most with one-time recordings, such as events, where a retake is impossible.\n\nAfter the event, the editor could still adjust voices, world audio, avatar sounds, and so on without being locked into a single mixed track.\n\nA simple version would already help: keep the current mixed output for normal listening, and optionally send individual buses to additional devices.\n\nEven routing only some buses separately would be useful.\n\nThank you for considering this when time allows.",
